1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,200
These are Qb and Qbo.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,600
My camera can't tell them apart.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,400
Last week, it decided this ball was Qbo,

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,600
for twenty-six minutes.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,800
I work all day.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,600
I just want to know simple things:

7
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,000
did my cats eat, sleep, play?

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,400
Cats hide illness, so small changes

9
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:20,800
matter.

10
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,400
Why not send every frame to an AI?

11
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,200
One camera makes over a hundred and

12
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,200
seventy thousand frames a day.

13
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,200
That's about sixty-three thousand dollars

14
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,000
a year.

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,800
A tiny model on a Raspberry Pi is almost

16
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,800
free, but it makes mistakes.

17
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,800
So we built both.

18
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,200
The Pi watches every frame.

19
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,000
When it's unsure, it says exactly why.

20
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,000
It knows fourteen kinds of doubt, like:

21
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,800
I relabeled this cat by distance alone.

22
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,200
That doubt becomes a plain-English

23
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,200
question for Meta's Muse Spark.

24
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:11,000
The agent pulls the frames it needs,

25
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,800
compares the cats, and answers with a

26
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:14,200
reason.

27
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:15,600
Watch.

28
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,600
Cool white, thin upright tail.

29
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,600
This is Qb, not Qbo.

30
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,000
Overturned.

31
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,200
Related doubts get reviewed together,

32
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,800
fetching each image once.

33
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,400
Twelve questions, three calls.

34
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,000
Here, the tracker kept painting Qbo onto

35
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,800
Qb's spot after Qbo had walked away.

36
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,400
The agent saw no Qbo there, and cut the

37
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:41,800
guesses.

38
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,600
Every verdict rewrites the record, and

39
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,200
every change is traceable.

40
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,000
Then memory.

41
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,800
Not boxes and timestamps, but a diary:

42
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,600
Qb slept in the green bed, four

43
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,200
thirty-four to four forty.

44
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,000
Over weeks, it learns what normal looks

45
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,800
like for each cat, in each spot.

46
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,000
The numbers:

47
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,800
twelve doubts in eight minutes, less than

48
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,400
one percent of frames.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,200
Twenty-six cents to review them, about a

50
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:20,400
fifth of the cost of sending every frame

51
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,600
to the AI.

52
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,800
And only those frames ever leave my home.

53
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:29,600
Next:

54
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:32,400
catch more errors, run full days, and

55
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:35,600
teach the Pi from what the agent learns.

56
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,200
Cats are just the start.

57
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:42,000
Any camera watching for rare moments, like

58
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,800
an elderly parent, wildlife or a factory

59
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,800
line, has the same gap.

60
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,000
Our answer:

61
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,200
cheap eyes on every frame, a smart brain

62
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:55,400
only when it matters, and a memory that

63
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,200
keeps growing.

64
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:59,000
Built this week, on Meta's Muse Spark.
